}
```

Explanation:

- `fgets(..., sizeof(line), stdin)` reads a line of input from standard input (the terminal) until it reaches the end of the line or encounters an end-of-file character (`'\n'`), storing it in `line`.
- `printf("Received: %s\n", line);` prints the line received.

Both solutions ensure you can read a single character from the terminal without needing to manually handle the newline character.

